# {{display}}

A browser extension written in Rust with [oxichrome](https://oxichrome.dev). One codebase builds for Chrome and Firefox.

## Build and load

```sh
cargo oxichrome build                    # writes dist/chromium
cargo oxichrome build --target firefox   # writes dist/firefox
```

- **Chrome:** open `chrome://extensions`, turn on Developer mode, click **Load unpacked** and pick `dist/chromium`.
- **Firefox:** open `about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox`, click **Load Temporary Add-on** and pick `dist/firefox/manifest.json`.

Build again after a change, then press the reload button on the extension's card.

## What's here

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
#if !minimal
| `src/lib.rs` | `#[extension]`: the name, version, permissions, icons and toolbar button. The manifest is generated from it. |
#endif
#if background
| `src/background.rs` | The background service worker: `#[background]` runs when it starts, `#[on(...)]` handles browser events.{{settings_note}} |
#endif
#if minimal
| `src/lib.rs` | `#[extension]`: the name, version, icons and toolbar button, which the manifest is generated from. The background service worker lives here too: `#[background]` runs when it starts, `#[on(...)]` handles browser events. |
#endif
#if popup
| `src/popup.rs` | `#[popup]`: what opens when you click the toolbar button, written as a [Leptos](https://leptos.dev) component. |
#endif
#if options
| `src/options.rs` | `#[options_page]`: the settings page, opened from the gear in the popup or the browser's extensions page. |
#endif
#if side_panel
| `src/side_panel.rs` | `#[side_panel]`: a panel that stays open next to the page (Firefox calls it the sidebar). |
#endif
#if content_script
| `src/content_script.rs` | `#[content_script]`: runs inside matching pages. Open https://example.com to see it. |
#endif
#if ui
| `static/` | Stylesheets and icons, copied into `dist/` as they are. `base.css` holds the shared look; change colors in `style.css`. |
#endif
#if !ui
| `static/` | The icons and any other files the extension needs, copied into `dist/` as they are. |
#endif
#if i18n
| `static/_locales/en/messages.json` | The extension's text. Add a folder like `_locales/de` with the same keys to translate it; `t!(key)` picks the right language. |
#endif

## Where to go next

Every browser API oxichrome covers has a working example in [examples/](https://github.com/0xsouravm/oxichrome/tree/main/examples):

| You want | Look at |
|---|---|
| Storage, the toolbar badge, a settings page | counter-extension |
| Tabs, windows, a side panel, keyboard shortcuts, right-click menus, translations | tab-tidy |
| Alarms, notifications, idle detection | focus-timer |
| Content scripts, messages, offscreen documents, downloads, asking for permissions | page-lens |
| Blocking requests, cookies, page loads | quiet-web |
| The address bar, search, top sites, bookmarks, history | launchpad |
| Calling a web API through wasm-bindgen | color-picker |

The full API reference is at [oxichrome.dev](https://oxichrome.dev).
